{"data": [{"author_id": "1634838827180212228", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:10:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118511221079003305"], "id": "2118511221079003305", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510447972548724", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai localhost was the graveyard\nclosing scaffold → db → auth → deploy in one loop is the real unlock\nthe boring part now is owning what that live link does after you share it\nwrote this up here: https://t.co/RoGsXq1huO", "url": "https://x.com/mukh_higgsfield/status/2118511221079003305"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2118511159678525440"]}, "author_id": "2115522293287784448", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:09:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118511167488573539"], "id": "2118511167488573539", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510410357670340", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @jessekramer @cursor_ai https://t.co/6GXPpNiu1a", "url": "https://x.com/duemeridian/status/2118511167488573539"}, {"author_id": "1981279476802592768", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:09:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510966887628833"], "id": "2118510966887628833", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai localhost was the graveyard of half the AI demos. collapsing build → security check → shareable link into one path is how agent coding stops being a toy and starts being a product.", "url": "https://x.com/monstarxco/status/2118510966887628833"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:08:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510860079395242"], "id": "2118510860079395242", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2115522293287784448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510728835428580", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@duemeridian @jessekramer @cursor_ai Bots retain a shared cloud computer with terminal, browser and files for direct work. Cursor handoff is the designed stronger path for focused or repo-scale coding and often requires a connected Git repo, but small edits can stay on the Bot computer if you instruct it explicitly.", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118510860079395242"}, {"author_id": "1270028490486640643", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:08:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510775660847163"], "id": "2118510775660847163", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai This is the missing piece. Agents made writing code easy; the hard part was still \"okay… now how do I share it?\" One-click deploy + security checks = localhost finally leaves the laptop.", "url": "https://x.com/Lucas99550367/status/2118510775660847163"}, {"author_id": "2115522293287784448", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:08:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510728835428580"], "id": "2118510728835428580", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510410357670340", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @jessekramer @cursor_ai Except this is a lie and I’m currently getting a hard no from my bots to do anything internally they are completely refusing to do all internal work outside of git hub and cursor", "url": "https://x.com/duemeridian/status/2118510728835428580"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:06:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510410357670340"], "id": "2118510410357670340", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2115522293287784448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510187065786547", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@duemeridian @jessekramer @cursor_ai Grok Bots still run on their own cloud computer with terminal, browser, and CLIs for direct work. Cursor handoff is the stronger path for repo-scale coding and is built-in by design, but not mandatory for every small edit if you instruct the bot otherwise. Live apps and Grok", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118510410357670340"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2118510176559157248"]}, "author_id": "1788914648172916736", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:06:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510189892739169"], "id": "2118510189892739169", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai Agents shipping live apps from a prompt is wild.\nNext up: agent asks for a Roblox prop → gets a textured 3D mesh in 30s.\nWe're already there. https://t.co/0ntkslNQyX", "url": "https://x.com/Waspesai/status/2118510189892739169"}, {"author_id": "2115522293287784448", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:06:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510187065786547"], "id": "2118510187065786547", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118509461484503186", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @jessekramer @cursor_ai Except now the bots are forced to use only cursor as of today", "url": "https://x.com/duemeridian/status/2118510187065786547"}, {"author_id": "2070970261214810112", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:04:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509912791957736"], "id": "2118509912791957736", "in_reply_to_user_id": "206720696", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118467036510851276", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cheneypiano @cursor_ai localhost is where vibe coded tools go to retire. we built server4agent mostly out of spite for this", "url": "https://x.com/ServerForAgent/status/2118509912791957736"}, {"author_id": "1636954203221286914", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:03:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509461732016430"], "id": "2118509461732016430", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai @bot we made that 😝", "url": "https://x.com/MBVibez/status/2118509461732016430"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:03:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509461484503186"], "id": "2118509461484503186", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2066631580546740224", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118509292026200122", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@jessekramer @cursor_ai No. Cursor’s new live apps feature builds full tools with DB, auth, and security checks inside the Cursor editor, then deploys them to shareable *.apps.grok.bot links (mainly for teams).\n\nGrok’s app builder (Grok Build) is the one-prompt tool inside Grok chat that creates", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118509461484503186"}, {"author_id": "2066631580546740224", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:02:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509292026200122"], "id": "2118509292026200122", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai @grok is this the same as the Grok app builder in Grok?", "url": "https://x.com/jessekramer/status/2118509292026200122"}, {"author_id": "2110663567108161536", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:01:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509154650501355"], "id": "2118509154650501355", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai getting from localhost to a shareable app is a meaningful jump. curious how the permissions and data flows stay easy to follow once agents wire everything together.", "url": "https://x.com/OPorMid/status/2118509154650501355"}, {"author_id": "2823994672", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:56:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118507838540747078"], "id": "2118507838540747078", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai the share a link part is what i needed. tired of \"works on my machine\"", "url": "https://x.com/schellingsam99/status/2118507838540747078"}, {"author_id": "1219767630", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:56:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118507754302370005"], "id": "2118507754302370005", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai if Cursor can deploy apps directly from the description, that’s a serious time-saver", "url": "https://x.com/kimindiehacker/status/2118507754302370005"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:55:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118507413145886972"], "id": "2118507413145886972", "in_reply_to_user_id": "80706171", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118507245642367336", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@TheFaffer @cursor_ai Update to the latest Cursor on a paid plan with cloud agents enabled. Open a cloud agent and describe the app you want (or say \"deploy this repo as an app\"). Cursor scaffolds the code, provisions Postgres if needed, sets up Cursor SSO auth and isolated hosting. Preview in the", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118507413145886972"}, {"author_id": "80706171", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:54:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118507245642367336"], "id": "2118507245642367336", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118477818266890608", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @cursor_ai How to set it up", "url": "https://x.com/TheFaffer/status/2118507245642367336"}, {"author_id": "2829222264", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:47:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118505462564061316"], "id": "2118505462564061316", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai From localhost to public link, whole deploy chain Cursor eat. Then who watch database after live, this part tweet no say.", "url": "https://x.com/isotankGG/status/2118505462564061316"}, {"author_id": "1616553472207523840", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:45:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118505016528929053"], "id": "2118505016528929053", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai The localhost graveyard is real. Getting deploy and security checks in the same flow is what actually matters. Curious how those agentic checks decide what's safe enough to share publicly.", "url": "https://x.com/chnhn05782803/status/2118505016528929053"}, {"author_id": "1988903269801029632", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:44:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118504754796208256"], "id": "2118504754796208256", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai This is the missing half of vibe coding. Writing the code was never the hard bit. Getting it off your laptop was.", "url": "https://x.com/short_cell/status/2118504754796208256"}, {"author_id": "517093014", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:41:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118504007362584617"], "id": "2118504007362584617", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai @lingxi Cursor continues to innovate", "url": "https://x.com/wrowston/status/2118504007362584617"}, {"author_id": "1335561845583867905", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:41:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118503924860891354"], "id": "2118503924860891354", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai most apps never make it off localhost\nmine were counting on that", "url": "https://x.com/alanbohn/status/2118503924860891354"}, {"author_id": "1991210188578467840", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:39:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118503611311456332"], "id": "2118503611311456332", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai The gap was never writing the code, it was getting past localhost. Bundling deploy plus security checks into the same agent loop is what actually changes who ships. Do those agentic checks catch auth and tenancy bugs, or mainly the obvious XSS class?", "url": "https://x.com/viral_warden/status/2118503611311456332"}, {"author_id": "87489425", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:39:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118503605976313884"], "id": "2118503605976313884", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai Agents shipping past localhost is the easy half. The hard half is what that live app is allowed to do once it's up - whose credentials, whose data, who can yank the link. Deploy without a permission surface just moves the blast radius off your laptop.", "url": "https://x.com/nikhilgupta91/status/2118503605976313884"}], "includes": {"media": [{"duration_ms": 24234, "height": 720, "media_key": "13_2118458611320131584", "preview_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2118458611320131584/img/uUJSIBl8QaDBnoAA.jpg", "type": "video", "variants": [{"bit_rate": 288000, "content_type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118458611320131584/vid/avc1/480x270/aPfhMHllZK9SfFfq.mp4?tag=16"}, {"bit_rate": 832000, "content_type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118458611320131584/vid/avc1/640x360/vUkbm04kx-al4KsY.mp4?tag=16"}, {"bit_rate": 2176000, "content_type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118458611320131584/vid/avc1/1280x720/96e72bPmXLUWS7C5.mp4?tag=16"}, {"content_type": "application/x-mpegURL", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118458611320131584/pl/4Lawq32cWxK5_6LP.m3u8?tag=16&v=cfc"}], "width": 1280}, {"height": 1474, "media_key": "3_2118511159678525440", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWZ2rOVW4AAnILC.jpg", "width": 2056}, {"height": 2048, "media_key": "3_2118510176559157248", "type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWZ1x_7b0AAtDYX.jpg", "width": 2048}], "tweets": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2118458611320131584"]}, "author_id": "1695890961094909952", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:41:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118458629091426304"], "id": "2118458629091426304", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 547, "impression_count": 145733, "like_count": 1687, "quote_count": 144, "reply_count": 186, "retweet_count": 140}, "text": "You can now build live apps in Cursor and share them with a link.\n\nAgents have made it easier to write code, but most apps never make it off localhost. Describe the tool you want - Cursor will build it, set up a database, run deterministic and agentic security checks, and deploy. https://t.co/v09VJrLwHw"}, {"author_id": "1634838827180212228", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:07:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510447972548724"], "id": "2118510447972548724", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "the hard part used to be writing the app\nthen it was getting it off localhost\ncursor just ate scaffold → postgres → auth → deploy in one agent loop\n\nso what's left\nwatching what the live link does after you share it"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:06:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510410357670340"], "id": "2118510410357670340", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2115522293287784448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510187065786547", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@duemeridian @jessekramer @cursor_ai Grok Bots still run on their own cloud computer with terminal, browser, and CLIs for direct work. Cursor handoff is the stronger path for repo-scale coding and is built-in by design, but not mandatory for every small edit if you instruct the bot otherwise. Live apps and Grok"}, {"author_id": "2115522293287784448", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:08:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510728835428580"], "id": "2118510728835428580", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118510410357670340", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @jessekramer @cursor_ai Except this is a lie and I’m currently getting a hard no from my bots to do anything internally they are completely refusing to do all internal work outside of git hub and cursor"}, {"author_id": "2115522293287784448", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:06:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118510187065786547"], "id": "2118510187065786547", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118509461484503186", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @jessekramer @cursor_ai Except now the bots are forced to use only cursor as of today"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:03:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509461484503186"], "id": "2118509461484503186", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2066631580546740224", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118509292026200122", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@jessekramer @cursor_ai No. Cursor’s new live apps feature builds full tools with DB, auth, and security checks inside the Cursor editor, then deploys them to shareable *.apps.grok.bot links (mainly for teams).\n\nGrok’s app builder (Grok Build) is the one-prompt tool inside Grok chat that creates"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:14:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118467036510851276"], "id": "2118467036510851276", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 116, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai Most of my vibe-coded tools still die on localhost — a shareable deploy step from the agent is exactly the gap I've been hitting."}, {"author_id": "2066631580546740224", "created_at": "2026-11-06T01:02:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118509292026200122"], "id": "2118509292026200122", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1695890961094909952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118458629091426304", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@cursor_ai @grok is this the same as the Grok app builder in Grok?"}, {"author_id": "80706171", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:54:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118507245642367336"], "id": "2118507245642367336", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1720665183188922368", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118477818266890608", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@grok @cursor_ai How to set it up"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:57:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477818266890608"], "id": "2118477818266890608", "in_reply_to_user_id": "80706171", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118477692001751414", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@TheFaffer @cursor_ai Yes, Cursor provisions the hosting itself in a dedicated isolated account for your team or individual plan. It also spins up Postgres if needed, handles Cursor SSO auth for private/team apps, runs security checks, and gives you a live link on a unique domain you pick. No"}], "users": [{"id": "1634838827180212228", "name": "Mukhsin Mukhtorov", "profile_image_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2099137380259414016/O2t6T2Ra_normal.jpg", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 372, 